.SH "Electron-to-Chromium \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP\fR\fP"
.PP
This repository provides a mapping of Electron versions to the Chromium version that it uses\&.

.PP
This package is used in \fRBrowserslist\fP, so you can use e\&.g\&. \fRelectron >= 1\&.4\fP in \fRAutoprefixer\fP, \fRStylelint\fP, \fRbabel-preset-env\fP and \fReslint-plugin-compat\fP\&.

.PP
\fBSupported by:\fP

.PP
\fR \fP
.SS "Install"
Install using \fRnpm install electron-to-chromium\fP\&.
.SS "Usage"
To include Electron-to-Chromium, require it:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var e2c = require('electron\-to\-chromium');
.fi
.PP
.SS "Properties"
The Electron-to-Chromium object has 4 properties to use:
.SS "\fRversions\fP"
An object of key-value pairs with a \fImajor\fP Electron version as the key, and the corresponding major Chromium version as the value\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var versions = e2c\&.versions;
console\&.log(versions['1\&.4']);
// returns "53"
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRfullVersions\fP"
An object of key-value pairs with a Electron version as the key, and the corresponding full Chromium version as the value\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var versions = e2c\&.fullVersions;
console\&.log(versions['1\&.4\&.11']);
// returns "53\&.0\&.2785\&.143"
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRchromiumVersions\fP"
An object of key-value pairs with a \fImajor\fP Chromium version as the key, and the corresponding major Electron version as the value\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var versions = e2c\&.chromiumVersions;
console\&.log(versions['54']);
// returns "1\&.4"
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRfullChromiumVersions\fP"
An object of key-value pairs with a Chromium version as the key, and an array of the corresponding major Electron versions as the value\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var versions = e2c\&.fullChromiumVersions;
console\&.log(versions['54\&.0\&.2840\&.101']);
// returns ["1\&.5\&.1", "1\&.5\&.0"]
.fi
.PP
 
.SS "Functions"
.SS "\fRelectronToChromium(query)\fP"
Arguments:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Query: string or number, required\&. A major or full Electron version\&.
.PP

.PP
A function that returns the corresponding Chromium version for a given Electron function\&. Returns a string\&.

.PP
If you provide it with a major Electron version, it will return a major Chromium version:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var chromeVersion = e2c\&.electronToChromium('1\&.4');
// chromeVersion is "53"
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you provide it with a full Electron version, it will return the full Chromium version\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var chromeVersion = e2c\&.electronToChromium('1\&.4\&.11');
// chromeVersion is "53\&.0\&.2785\&.143"
.fi
.PP

.PP
If a query does not match a Chromium version, it will return \fRundefined\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var chromeVersion = e2c\&.electronToChromium('9000');
// chromeVersion is undefined
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRchromiumToElectron(query)\fP"
Arguments:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Query: string or number, required\&. A major or full Chromium version\&.
.PP

.PP
Returns a string with the corresponding Electron version for a given Chromium query\&.

.PP
If you provide it with a major Chromium version, it will return a major Electron version:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var electronVersion = e2c\&.chromiumToElectron('54');
// electronVersion is "1\&.4"
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you provide it with a full Chrome version, it will return an array of full Electron versions\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var electronVersions = e2c\&.chromiumToElectron('56\&.0\&.2924\&.87');
// electronVersions is ["1\&.6\&.3", "1\&.6\&.2", "1\&.6\&.1", "1\&.6\&.0"]
.fi
.PP

.PP
If a query does not match an Electron version, it will return \fRundefined\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var electronVersion = e2c\&.chromiumToElectron('10');
// electronVersion is undefined
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRelectronToBrowserList(query)\fP \fBDEPRECATED\fP"
Arguments:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Query: string or number, required\&. A major Electron version\&.
.PP

.PP
\fI\fBDeprecated\fP: Browserlist already includes electron-to-chromium\&.\fP

.PP
A function that returns a \fRBrowserslist\fP query that matches the given major Electron version\&. Returns a string\&.

.PP
If you provide it with a major Electron version, it will return a Browserlist query string that matches the Chromium capabilities:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var query = e2c\&.electronToBrowserList('1\&.4');
// query is "Chrome >= 53"
.fi
.PP

.PP
If a query does not match a Chromium version, it will return \fRundefined\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var query = e2c\&.electronToBrowserList('9000');
// query is undefined
.fi
.PP
.SS "Importing just versions, fullVersions, chromiumVersions and fullChromiumVersions"
All lists can be imported on their own, if file size is a concern\&.
.SS "\fRversions\fP"
.PP
.nf
var versions = require('electron\-to\-chromium/versions');
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRfullVersions\fP"
.PP
.nf
var fullVersions = require('electron\-to\-chromium/full\-versions');
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRchromiumVersions\fP"
.PP
.nf
var chromiumVersions = require('electron\-to\-chromium/chromium\-versions');
.fi
.PP
.SS "\fRfullChromiumVersions\fP"
.PP
.nf
var fullChromiumVersions = require('electron\-to\-chromium/full\-chromium\-versions');
.fi
.PP
.SS "Updating"
This package will be updated with each new Electron release\&.

.PP
To update the list, run \fRnpm run build\&.js\fP\&. Requires internet access as it downloads from the canonical list of Electron versions\&.

.PP
To verify correct behaviour, run \fRnpm test\fP\&.
